  "response": "**Setup:**\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002, P(¬D) = 0.998\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(−|¬D) = 0.95 → P(+|¬D) = 0.05\n\n**Bayes' theorem:**\n\nP(D|+) = [P(+|D)·P(D)] / [P(+|D)·P(D) + P(+|¬D)·P(¬D)]\n\n= (0.98 × 0.002) / (0.98 × 0.002 + 0.05 × 0.998)\n\n= 0.00196 / (0.00196 + 0.0499)\n\n= 0.00196 / 0.05186\n\n≈ 0.037794 → **3.78%**\n\nSo despite the test being fairly accurate, because the condition is rare, most positive results are false positives — there's only about a 3.78% chance the person actually has the condition.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
